From 2840fc5c074c5387f1bf0f99118df19ded831e7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:05:15 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/4] KVM: s390: Add ESA/390 address translation and shadow
 gmaps

Add a walker for ESA/390 segment and page tables and use it for the
guest accesses KVM makes while a vCPU in the ESA/390-compatibility mode
has the DAT bit in its PSW, in the primary or the home space. Present
segment- and page-translation exceptions in ESA/390 format.

Add a kind of shadow gmap for an ESA/390 address space. Its addresses
are the virtual addresses after prefixing, it is keyed by segment-table
designation and prefix, and it is filled by the same walker. Table pages
are not write-protected: like a TLB, the shadow keeps a translation until
the guest purges it. For INVALIDATE PAGE TABLE ENTRY, an rmap leads from
each guest page-table page to the shadow segments made from it, including
the pages prefixing moves to another segment. Changes of the parent mapping
remove shadow entries as for vsie shadows. A page the guest may store
into is mapped writable at once, as for real spaces.

Nothing creates such a shadow yet.
